    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1052c-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If ASIC considers that AFCA has not done all things reasonably practicable to ensure compliance with:  (a) the mandatory requirements for the AFCA scheme under section 1051; or  (b) a condition of the authorisation of the AFCA scheme imposed by the Minister under paragraph 1050(5)(b); or  (c) regulatory requirements issued under section 1052A; ASIC may give AFCA written notice that it intends to give AFCA a specified direction under this section." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If ASIC considers that AFCA has not done all things reasonably practicable to ensure compliance with:  (a) the mandatory requirements for the AFCA scheme under section 1051; or  (b) a condition of the authorisation of the AFCA scheme imposed by the Minister under paragraph 1050(5)(b); or  (c) regulatory requirements issued under section 1052A; ASIC may give AFCA written notice that it intends to give AFCA a specified direction under this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c2689df56d5375e1d2a53e163673b6590d594127edc840aa7935f581dc0f6659" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1052c ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ASIC may give AFCA a specified direction if it considers non-compliance with mandatory requirements or regulatory conditions." ;
