concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1054C Reference of questions of law to Federal Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1054c ;
    values:originalText "(1) AFCA may, on its own initiative or on the request of a party to a superannuation complaint, refer a question of law arising in relation to the making of a determination relating to the complaint to the Federal Court for decision.  (2) The Federal Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine a question of law referred to it under this section.  (3) If a question of law has been so referred to the Federal Court, AFCA must not:  Schedule 1  External dispute resolution" ;
    skos:definition "(1) AFCA may, on its own initiative or on the request of a party to a superannuation complaint, refer a question of law arising in relation to the making of a determination relating to the complaint to the Federal Court for decision.  (2) The Federal Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine a question of law referred to it under this section.  (3) If a question of law has been so referred to the Federal Court, AFCA must not:  Schedule 1  External dispute resolution"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c02b87d5606b3aec45c419c3ab87bcf9dffcb62c5a6c6b722867ada6c6a510c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer ;
