doc:sch-1-sec-1055-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1055(3) Making a determination" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) AFCA must affirm a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit if AFCA is satisfied that the decision, in its operation in relation to:  (a) the complainant; and  (b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party to the complaint; was fair and reasonable in all the circumstances. Varying etc. decisions or conduct" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1055(4) Making a determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  (a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant; or  (b) conduct; is unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or more of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the purpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  (a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant; or  (b) conduct; is unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or more of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the purpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "78c2ae2c7c4f9e34d451b3681293c77367f73c7d770a816f05dd9c9a73189620" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055 ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "AFCA may take actions to place a complainant in a position where unfairness or unreasonableness no longer exists." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
