doc:sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1055(4) Making a determination" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  (a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant; or  (b) conduct; is unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or more of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the purpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists." ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1055(5) Making a determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If AFCA is satisfied that a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit, in its operation in relation to:  (a) the complainant; and  (b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party to the complaint; is unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or more of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the purpose of placing the complainant (and any other person so joined as a party), as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If AFCA is satisfied that a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit, in its operation in relation to:  (a) the complainant; and  (b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party to the complaint; is unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or more of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the purpose of placing the complainant (and any other person so joined as a party), as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1126d0a7b9b439e8e94fb8d8888260bc362705941593aa6b5267d27acb174d69" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055 ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "AFCA may take actions to place complainant in a position where unfairness/unreasonableness no longer exists." ;
