    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the note, substitute: Note: If a person is dissatisfied with a statement given to the Commissioner by a superannuation provider under section 390-5 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953, the person may make a complaint: (a) under the AFCA scheme (within the meaning of Chapter 7 of the Corporations Act 2001), but not before the authorisation of the scheme comes into force; or (b) under section 15CA of the Superannuation (Resolution of Complaints) Act 1993, but not on or after the day on or after which complaints cannot be made because of section 14AB of that Act. Retirement Savings Accounts Act 1997" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Subsection 95(1A)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1A) If it appears to ASIC that an RSA provider has refused or failed to give effect to:  (a) a determination of the Superannuation Complaints Tribunal under sections 37D to 37G of the Superannuation (Resolution of Complaints) Act 1993; or  (b) a determination made under the AFCA scheme (within the meaning of Chapter 7 of the Corporations Act 2001);  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying once the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution scheme comes into force  Part 2  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  ASIC may, by written notice, tell the RSA provider that ASIC proposes to conduct an investigation of the whole or a part of the affairs of the RSA provider." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1A) If it appears to ASIC that an RSA provider has refused or failed to give effect to:  (a) a determination of the Superannuation Complaints Tribunal under sections 37D to 37G of the Superannuation (Resolution of Complaints) Act 1993; or  (b) a determination made under the AFCA scheme (within the meaning of Chapter 7 of the Corporations Act 2001);  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying once the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution scheme comes into force  Part 2  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  ASIC may, by written notice, tell the RSA provider that ASIC proposes to conduct an investigation of the whole or a part of the affairs of the RSA provider."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ec49bd87521e50a2b90fafadd679b46f2166a365e25fceaef8c72987419cb46b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ASIC may tell RSA provider that ASIC proposes to conduct an investigation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
