doc:sch-1-sec-16 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16 Subsection 95(1A)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1A) If it appears to ASIC that an RSA provider has refused or failed to give effect to:  (a) a determination of the Superannuation Complaints Tribunal under sections 37D to 37G of the Superannuation (Resolution of Complaints) Act 1993; or  (b) a determination made under the AFCA scheme (within the meaning of Chapter 7 of the Corporations Act 2001);  External dispute resolution  Schedule 1 Amendments applying once the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution scheme comes into force  Part 2  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  ASIC may, by written notice, tell the RSA provider that ASIC proposes to conduct an investigation of the whole or a part of the affairs of the RSA provider." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

