doc:sch-2-sec-9 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9 Subsections 101(1) and (1A)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) Each trustee of a regulated superannuation fund other than a self managed superannuation fund, or of an approved deposit fund:  (b) must have an internal dispute resolution procedure that complies with the standards, and requirements, mentioned in subparagraph 912A(2)(a)(i) of the Corporations Act 2001 in relation to financial services licensees; and  (c) must give to ASIC the same information as the trustee would be required to give under subparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of the Corporations Act 2001 if the trustee were a financial services licensee; and  (d) must ensure that written reasons are given, in accordance with requirements specified under subsection (1B) of this  Internal dispute resolution  Schedule 2  Treasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the Australian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018 Compilation date: 10/08/2022 Registered: 25/08/2022  section, for any decision of the trustee (or failure by the trustee to make a decision) relating to a complaint. Note:" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Transitional provision for giving written reasons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "Until the first time an instrument made under subsection 101(1B) of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 as amended by this Part comes into force, paragraph 101(1)(d) of that Act as so amended has effect as if:  (a) the requirements of paragraphs 101(1)(c) to (e) of that Act as in force immediately before the commencement of this Part were the requirements specified under subsection 101(1B) of that Act as so amended; and  (b) subsection 101(1A) of that Act as in force immediately before that commencement still had effect." ;
    skos:definition "Until the first time an instrument made under subsection 101(1B) of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 as amended by this Part comes into force, paragraph 101(1)(d) of that Act as so amended has effect as if:  (a) the requirements of paragraphs 101(1)(c) to (e) of that Act as in force immediately before the commencement of this Part were the requirements specified under subsection 101(1B) of that Act as so amended; and  (b) subsection 101(1A) of that Act as in force immediately before that commencement still had effect."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8fc97970c180e2a0a352bce2dea11099ede02599ebeb172f59e973f94772e976" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Transitional provision for giving written reasons" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2022c00235.pdf> ;
